# Production host login

The Unix account `deploy` in `docs/ops/INFRASTRUCTURE.md` and `docs/ops/DEPLOYMENT.md` is the watchdog and application runtime identity. It is not an agent shell.

- The only SSH login an agent may use is `observe` (`ssh observe@84.32.48.2`).
- Use that session for journal and readiness inspection.
- If `observe` is unreachable, stop. Do not fall back to `deploy` or `root`.
- Do not run `systemctl start|stop|restart|kill`, `deploy.sh`, `engine-bluegreen.sh`, or `apitoken-watchdog retry|run`.
- Land releases with `git push` and `./deploy/agent-merge.sh`. The host watchdog performs cutovers.

```bash
# BAD — caused the 2026-08-22 outage
ssh deploy@84.32.48.2 'sudo systemctl restart claude-api-anthropic@8787'

# GOOD — live logs only
ssh observe@84.32.48.2

# GOOD — deploy
./deploy/agent-merge.sh
```
